A||||2||fiero56||'87 Duke Coupe stuttering under low rpm load||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||12-09-2001||11:14 AM||||I took delivery of an '87 auto coupe with 108K miles yesterday. On the drive home on the highway while going up a moderate hill the car starts really stuttering and attempting to backfire. While this is happening, the engine is really lacking in power. This no happens anytime the engine is under a light to moderate load while in 3rd gear. It now happens in town while in 3rd  anywhere at 35mph+. It does not happen when pulling from a stop, the engine pulls strong and smooth from a stop. The stuttering becomes noticeable in 2nd, and terrible in 3rd. I figure it has to do with ignition, as this stuttering is very instantaneous. All wire connectios are good, all vac lines are good. I did find that the EGR valve will not hold a vacuum. Is this a probable cause? I am replacing it asap, but is this probable cause?<P>This is my first auto, and my first Duke, all in one, so I'm lost in the engine bay.||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||12-09-2001||12:23 PM||||Sounds like you have a bad spark plug wire. or spark plug (gap to large).||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||12-09-2001||05:14 PM||||I finally decided to just replace the plugs and wires to eliminate possibilities.  I had inspected and reinspected each plug 3 times. But while replacing the plugs with new ones, the electrode for cyl#2 was missing(it wasn't missing ealier in the day). New plugs and wires later, and it appears the problem is fixed.||||reg||1
